  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district council, polled 31 May 1911: six contests. \"The Newry No. 2 Rural District Council now consists of the following 24 elected members (two for each division)\" (Newry Reporter, 3 June 1911, p. 7). No party labels are printed. Polled 31 May 1911; declared on Thursday 1 June at the Newry Workhouse by W. R. Bell, deputy returning officer. Two seats; the figures are the candidate totals. Kenny was the sitting member and was defeated; W. J. Gibson did not seek re-election. 191 votes recorded (none spoilt) of 233 on the register."
